  {
   "id": "yoma.26a.12",
   "daf": "26a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "הָרְבִיעִי חֲדָשִׁים עִם יְשָׁנִים וְכוּ׳. מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כְּרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב. דִּתְנַן, רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב אוֹמֵר: הַמַּעֲלֶה אֵיבָרִים לַכֶּבֶשׁ, הוּא מַעֲלֶה אוֹתָן לַמִּזְבֵּחַ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «The fourth» lottery was open to those «new» to the service along «with» those «old» hands who had already performed it, to determine who would take the limbs up from the ramp to the altar. The Gemara states: «The mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov. As we learned» in a mishna in tractate Tamid that «Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov says:» The priest «who takes the limbs up to the ramp is the one who takes them up» from the ramp «to the altar.» In contrast, according to the mishna discussed here, it is implied that a different priest won the privilege for the latter service in the lottery."
  }
 ],
